# Answer key for M4 (m4_semi_structured.sql): semi-structured shipment documents.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE (2026-10-07).
# CLOSED WORLD: every <result> column and every filter is stated. Conventions D-1..D-53.
#
# Row-deciding path: hdr JOIN shipment_line JOIN item_master, and the final WHERE. Every
# other CTE is LEFT joined: its own WHERE is a value of what it feeds (aggregated where it
# aggregates, D-45). A document column is the node for anything read out of it (D-29); a
# set-returning function in FROM is structural (D-27); an ordinality is an influence from
# its document or arrays (D-26, D-30); a series is derived from its bound columns (D-28).

@ 19 the whole statement

# --- main path ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
value lgx.shipment_line.shipment_line_id -> <result>.shipment_line_id identity
value lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.shipment_id identity
value lgx.shipment_header.header_attrs -> <result>.priority, <result>.delivery_window_start, <result>.first_contact_email, <result>.policy_no, <result>.service_level derived
note JSON_VALUE(... RETURNING text DEFAULT 'STD' ON EMPTY) reads the document only (D-29).
value lgx.shipment_line.line_attrs -> <result>.is_hazmat derived
value lgx.item_master.attrs, lgx.item_master.item_code -> <result>.item_doc derived
value lgx.shipment_line.shipped_qty, lgx.shipment_line.ordered_qty -> <result>.qty_pair derived

# --- charge_summary: jsonb_to_recordset, WHERE amount <> 0 -------------------------------------
value lgx.shipment_header.header_attrs -> <result>.freight_amount, <result>.charges_by_code, <result>.charge_count aggregated
influence lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.freight_amount, <result>.charges_by_code, <result>.charge_count
note charge_count is COUNT(*): its only value is charges' WHERE ch.amount, read out of the document (D-45, D-29).

# --- pkg_summary: JSON_TABLE with FOR ORDINALITY and EXISTS PATH -------------------------------
value lgx.shipment_header.header_attrs -> <result>.total_weight, <result>.void_count aggregated
influence lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.pkg_count, <result>.total_weight, <result>.void_count, <result>.max_pkg_ord
influence lgx.shipment_header.header_attrs -> <result>.max_pkg_ord
note MAX(pkg_ord): FOR ORDINALITY has no value, only the document's influence (D-30). pkg_count is COUNT(*): packages has no WHERE.
forbid value lgx.shipment_header.header_attrs -> <result>.pkg_count | JSON_TABLE in FROM is structural (D-27) and COUNT(*) reads nothing

# --- line_kv_summary: jsonb_each WITH ORDINALITY, WHERE key !~ '^_' -----------------------------
value lgx.shipment_line.line_attrs -> <result>.attr_keys, <result>.attrs_clean aggregated
influence lgx.shipment_line.shipment_line_id -> <result>.attr_keys, <result>.attrs_clean
influence lgx.shipment_line.line_attrs -> <result>.attr_keys
note array_agg(attr_key ORDER BY attr_ord): the ordinal, an influence of the document (D-26), orders the aggregate (B1 S11); D-47 lets line_attrs be both.

# --- tag_summary: multi-array unnest WITH ORDINALITY, WHERE tag IS NOT NULL ---------------------
value lgx.item_master.tags -> <result>.tag_list aggregated
influence lgx.item_master.tags, lgx.item_master.item_id -> <result>.tag_list
note The literal array ARRAY['A','B','C'] has no source; the ordinal's influence is from im.tags (D-26).

# --- promise_days: generate_series(promise_date, ship_date), WHERE on the series ---------------
value lgx.shipment_line.promise_date, lgx.shipment_line.ship_date -> <result>.business_days aggregated
influence lgx.shipment_line.shipment_line_id -> <result>.business_days
note COUNT(*): its value is the WHERE on g.d, which is derived from the series' bounds (D-28, D-45).

# --- calendar: ROWS FROM over literals -----------------------------------------------------------
forbid value lgx.shipment_line.ship_date -> <result>.holiday_flag | the calendar is literal series; the join key decides no value (D-28, D-5)
note holiday_flag reads no column.

# --- edi_summary: XMLTABLE + xpath(), WHERE doc_status ------------------------------------------
value lgx.edi_document.payload, lgx.edi_document.doc_status -> <result>.edi_qty, <result>.edi_orders aggregated
influence lgx.edi_document.payload -> <result>.edi_qty, <result>.edi_orders
note GROUP BY sku, a COLUMNS column derived from the document (D-30): the document is the grouping influence (D-47).
forbid filter lgx.edi_document.doc_status -> <result> | edi_summary is reached only through a LEFT join (D-45)

# --- ship_to_contact: jsonb_array_elements WITH ORDINALITY, DISTINCT ON on the null side ---------
value lgx.shipment_header.header_attrs -> <result>.ship_to_email conditional
influence lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.header_attrs -> <result>.ship_to_email
note email is read out of the document (derived) and the WHERE role = 'SHIP_TO' reads it too (conditional, D-45, D-51). DISTINCT ON key and ordering are influence (D-45): shipment_id, and the ordinal from the document.

# --- filters -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
filter lgx.shipment_header.header_attrs -> <result>
filter lgx.shipment_line.line_attrs -> <result>
